<title>MEXICO: BANCO DE MEXICO COMPLETES SECONDARY OPERATIONS.</title>
<headline>BANCO DE MEXICO COMPLETES SECONDARY OPERATIONS.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico on Wednesday placed all three direct sales of paper and five repurchase agreements throught which it sought to drain 2.930 billion pesos from the secondary market, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    351 days   20.91 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    175 days   20.89 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     85 days   19.86 pct</p>
<p>The amounts and maturities of the repurchase agreements were placed as follows:</p>
<p>    450 million     48 days   19.86 pct</p>
<p>    500 million     43 days   19.72 pct</p>
<p>    800 million     40 days   19.69 pct</p>
<p>    600 million	8 days   19.06 pct</p>
<p>    130 million	1 day    18.06 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
